o First Blood Part 2  the character transitioned from put-upon  antihero to full-on  agent of death the follow up saw Rambo  returning to Vietnam on a fact-finding  mission which eventually evolved into a  one versus everyone gunfight that seemed  to involve the entire country that film  also put up numbers at the box office  rendering the name Rambo  as shorthand for badass for the rest of  the decade and beyond thinks he's Rambo  Rambo is 1988's Rambo 3 moved the action  to Afghanistan and seemingly served as  an end to the series until 2008 two  decades after Rambo 3 Stallone returned  to work both sides of the camera in the  simply titled Rambo the fourth movie saw  our hero laying low minding his own  business as a snake catcher in Thailand  before being forced into action to  protect a group of missionaries from  corrupt Burmese soldiers while the  movies reviews were mixed franchise fans  mostly found it to be a satisfactory  continuation of Rambo story and we're  also blown away by its insane level of  bloody violence now comes Rambo 5  throughout the production of the series  his final installment Stallone is popped  up on Instagram to share set photos that  help sketch out the story among those  photos is a cowboy hat sporting Rambo  looking intense and a rainstorm another  with him riding a horse an image of  Rambo and his bow and arrow and a short  series highlighting the film's co-stars  helping to fill in some more details as  the movie's official synopsis which  helps to explain the cowboy hats  according to the summary Rainbow five  will see John Rambo living and working  on a ranch in Arizona but this is no  pastoral life  John's violent past has left him feeling  deeply troubled suffering from PTSD when  a longtime family friend informs him  that her granddaughter has gone missing  in Mexico he sets off with her to locate  the young woman the journey leads him to  uncover a ring of sex traffickers and  kidnappers led by a vicious crime lord  whom he must stop at all costs as we all  know being deeply troubled and  traumatized by combats has never kept  Rambo from bringing the pain in the past  and we don't see any reason why this  final outing would be any different  while no release date has been announced  Rambo 5 is expected to hit screen  sometime in 2019 but just because it's  the end of the line for the Vietnam vet  doesn't mean it won't be fun to watch  and draw last blood it sounds like it's  very depressing but it's an effect it's  a kid's film check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite stuff or  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single  one  [Music]
 

